Still 1.2.0. A tenth lamp, because nine were ambiguous.

On a helmet the first six lit and the last three did not, which could mean two opposite things: that a tap armed and never died away in time, or that the margin and the attack were reached in different milliseconds so nothing armed at all. "arm" is the lamp that tells those apart.

The tap panel also shows the best rise and height of the last second against the two thresholds, so a tap that falls short says by how much.
